Bundled conductors are widely used in Extra High Voltage (EHV) transmission lines. Using two or more sub-conductors per phase increases the effective radius (Geometric Mean Radius) of the conductor bundle without significantly increasing the overall conductor weight. An increase in the effective conductor radius produces the following advantages: <ul><li>Reduces the electric field intensity at the conductor surface.</li><li>Minimizes corona loss and audible noise.</li><li>Reduces radio and communication interference.</li><li>Improves the mechanical characteristics of the line by distributing mechanical stresses among multiple sub-conductors.</li></ul> Hence, bundled conductors improve the mechanical stability of EHV transmission lines. \[\boxed{
\text{(B)}\;
\text{Mechanical stability of the line}
}\]

